//
// The production decode path at 2 layers on NPU2: 4 tokens per dispatch,
// on-chip lm_head + sampler + feedback, growing KV. --synthetic-weights
// swaps the gated Llama embedding table for a seeded one with the same
// layout; the numpy oracle runs on that same table. The nightly component
// check covers the real weights at 16 layers. The test compiles the design
// to a full ELF with @iron.jit and dispatches it through pyxrt.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, xrt_python_bindings, xrt_python_ctrl_scratchpad_bo
//
// From an empty cache: the first tokens attend one partial KV block.
// RUN: env LLAMA_CHAIN_N=2 %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_chain_persist_grow_mh.py --synthetic-weights --start-pos 0 | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: building synthetic embed/final_norm
// CHECK: KV cache: PASS
// CHECK: chain_persist_grow_mh: 4/4 tokens PASS
//
// Two dispatches crossing a KV block boundary (position 63 to 64), with the
// NPU left idle past its autosuspend delay in between: the KV cache and the
// next seed carry over in DDR.
// RUN: env LLAMA_CHAIN_N=2 %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_chain_persist_grow_mh.py --synthetic-weights --start-pos 62 --dispatches 2 --idle-s 6 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CARRY
// CARRY-COUNT-2: KV cache: PASS
// CARRY: chain_persist_grow_mh: 8/8 tokens PASS
// CARRY: carry across 2 dispatches: PASS
//
// Three of the four token slots, against the same three tokens one per
// dispatch: the records, the KV cache and the stage are byte-identical, and
// the slots that do not run move nothing.
// RUN: env LLAMA_CHAIN_N=2 %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_chain_persist_grow_mh.py --synthetic-weights --start-pos 62 --passes 3 --split | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SPLIT
// SPLIT: KV cache: PASS
// SPLIT: chain_persist_grow_mh: 3/3 tokens PASS
// SPLIT: 3 tokens vs 3 x 1: PASS
